Clinical notes:
{"note_id": 50, "date": "2025-02-20", "note_type": "Breast Imaging Report", "content": "Screening mammogram on 2025-02-06 showed a developing asymmetry in the upper outer left breast. Diagnostic mammogram with tomosynthesis and targeted ultrasound demonstrate an irregular hypoechoic mass measuring 2.1 x 1.8 x 1.6 cm at the 2 o'clock position, 5 cm from the nipple. A single morphologically abnormal left axillary lymph node is identified with cortical thickening to 4 mm. BI-RADS 5, highly suggestive of malignancy. Ultrasound-guided core biopsy was recommended and completed on 2025-02-20. No right breast abnormality."}
{"note_id": 51, "date": "2025-02-24", "note_type": "Pathology Report", "content": "SPECIMEN: Left breast, 2 o'clock, ultrasound-guided core needle biopsy.
DIAGNOSIS: Invasive ductal carcinoma, Nottingham grade 2 (tubule 3, nuclear 2, mitotic 1; total score 6 of 9). Associated ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate nuclear grade, comprising approximately 10% of the lesion. Lymphovascular invasion is not identified.
BIOMARKERS: ER positive (95%), PR positive (80%), HER2 negative by IHC (1+)."}
{"note_id": 52, "date": "2025-03-03", "note_type": "Surgical Oncology Consultation", "content": "Patient is a 58-year-old woman with newly diagnosed clinical T2 N1 invasive ductal carcinoma of the left breast. We discussed breast-conserving therapy versus mastectomy. Given tumor size relative to breast volume and patient preference, we plan left partial mastectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy. Staging workup with CT chest/abdomen/pelvis and bone scan shows no evidence of distant metastatic disease. Adjuvant radiation is anticipated after surgery."}
{"note_id": 53, "date": "2025-03-18", "note_type": "Operative Pathology Report", "content": "PROCEDURE: Left partial mastectomy with sentinel lymph node biopsy, 2025-03-18.
SPECIMEN A - LEFT BREAST, PARTIAL MASTECTOMY: Invasive ductal carcinoma, Nottingham grade 2, measuring 2.3 cm in greatest dimension. Margins negative; closest margin 4 mm (posterior). Lymphovascular invasion is present.
SPECIMEN B - LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODES: Three sentinel lymph nodes identified. One of three nodes positive for metastatic carcinoma with a 4.5 mm deposit; no extranodal extension.
PATHOLOGIC STAGE: pT2 pN1a."}

